    "breadcrumb": "Swing Catalyst atbalsts \u003e Aparatūra",
    "content": "Kalibrēšanas utilītas palaišana Lai lietotu jūsu līdzsvara plāksni, tai nepieciešams kalibrēšanas fails. Kalibrēšanas fails tiek izveidots katrai līdzsvara plāksnei, tāpēc neviens fails nav identisks. Ja jums nav instalēts kalibrēšanas fails, iespējams, ka jūsu plāksne nav reģistrēta garantijas nolūkiem. Šajā rakstā aplūkots kalibrēšanas faila iegūšanas un plāksnes reģistrācijas process.\nŠis raksts ir paredzēts nevēlama trokšņa noņemšanai un spiediena sadalījuma uzlabošanai līdzsvara plāksnei 3 un jaunākām versijām.\nLīdzsvara plāksne sastāv no 2048 augsta precizitātes spiediena sensoriem, un Sensor Edge Utility izmantošana plāksnes nullēšanai var būt nepieciešama, lai nodrošinātu labāko precizitāti. Šajā rakstā ir soli pa solim norādītas instrukcijas, kā nullēt līdzsvara plāksni.\nSVARĪGI!**\nŠim procesam ir divas daļas\ndaļa. Sensor Edge utilītas izmantošana, lai iegūtu jūsu plāksnes jaunāko kalibrēšanas failu.\ndaļa. Šī kalibrēšanas faila instalēšana SwingCatalyst programmā. Noteikti izlasiet visu šo atbalsta rakstu.\n1. daļa: SE utilītas izmantošana, lai iegūtu kalibrēšanas failu. Download the calibration utility\nIf asked to install drivers, click yes.\nConnect the plate to the computer.\nMake sure Swing Catalyst software is closed, SE Utility will not be able to detect your plate if Swing Catalyst is running.\nOpen the newly installed SE Utility\nFollow the instructions below.\nMake sure you have a monitor or TV connected to your computer so you can see the screen when standing on the Balance Plate.\nIf you have an older version installed please uninstall it first via Add or Remove Programs.\nClick Start:\nAfter clicking start it will automatically attempt to scan for devices, if it does not find your plate, click the drop down menu and select your Balance Plate.\nClick Scan Select the device that matches your plate’s serial number and click Next.\nRegistering your Balance Plate Example of filled out registration information Once you’ve filled out the required information for warranty and service purposes click Continue.\nIf possible select a camera and point it to show the Balance Plate, and click Next.\nA camera is not required though, you can still proceed if no camera is detected.\nMake sure to remove the carpet and any other objects from the Balance Plate, this is to ensure that the readings are not impacted by any external factors. Executing the calibration process Before stepping on the plate the utility collects data in order to have a baseline to compare to.\nPlease make sure you don’t accidentally stand on the plate until the utility instructs you to do so.\nPositioning It’s important that you stand on the plate as indicated by the utility.\nThe dark feet show where you should be standing, and the grey feet show where you should stand next.\nPlease follow each step as it is important to activate all of the regions of the plate.\nCompleted recording If you are not happy with the recording, perhaps you made a mistake? You can easily restart the process by clicking restart.\nClick Continue if you wish to proceed.\nClick the Save button then click the Send button\nBefore the data is sent to the manufacturer for review enter the approximate weight and usage.\nIn notes you can specify issues that you have with the plate, for example weak left foot, or other concerns.\nThe reason the manufacturer wishes to collect this data is to further improve the recalibration algorithms to provide more accurate sensor readings.\nEnter the information and click send:\nOnce finished the calibration file is saved to your Documents folder, press “No” and then close the utility.\nPart 2: Installing the calibration file Continue with these steps Start Swing Catalyst and go to Settings –\u003e Hardware in the main menu. The plate should be detected automatically, if not please see the troubleshooting section.\nClick the “Configure…” button to open the configuration dialog.\nSensor Plate Settings Go to the Stance Sensor tab, and click Browse and Install. Go to the directory you saved the calibration file, e.g: C:\\User\\YourUsername\\Documents and select the mxd file you just saved from the utility and click Open. When installation is completed it will let you know and you can click OK to close the windows.\nYour Balance Plate should now be ready to use. Start a new session in Swing Analysis and verify you get pressure readings in the Pressure and stance databox when capturing swings.\nNote: It may be necessary to run a re-calibration of your Balance Plate with heavy usage, this can be done by clicking the diagnostics button in Swing Catalyst Settings, which will launch the SE Utility.\nTroubleshooting The Balance Plate is not recognized or not showing as connected: Make sure the device is recognized by Windows. Open Windows device manager. How?\nVerify the **Sensor Edge **device is present under Ports (COM \u0026 LPT)\nIf it is not, or has a warning symbol, then try reinstalling the drivers and reconnecting the device to a different USB port.\nConnect the device to a different USB port on the computer.\nIf using a USB extender, try connecting the device to the PC without an extender.\nRestart Swing Catalyst.\nRestart the computer.\nIf you tried all these steps and it still shows as not connected in Swing Catalyst, please contact our support team.\nCalibration is not installed successfully The calibration file you received from the Sensor Edge Utility may be bad or the file may have become corrupted, try to run the utility again and install the new calibration file. If this doesn’t work, contact our support team. There is noise on the plate even though I’ve run the utility Noise can be present due several factors:\nWrong or no calibration file installed in Swing Catalyst.\nHeavy usage: The calibration utility should be run often, even once a month for heavily used plates.\nDirect exposure to sunlight.\nWear and tear on the sensors themselves.\nThe utility may not be able to filter out the noise if the signal to noise ratio is not good enough, the plate will in this case need to be recalibrated through an RMA. The manufacturer will then manually inspect the session that is generated by the utility to see if they can improve upon it.\nIf the manufacturer is unable to fix the issue and the plate is under warranty or ESA (extended service agreement), the plate can be shipped back to the manufacturer as long as an RMA is present.\nHardware incompatibilities Some issues have been seen with AMD 300-Series chipsets (AMD Ryzen 1700 / 2700 series ) with USB 1.1 devices. Specifically with the Balance Plate, where you only get 75 samples per second instead of ~145 samples per second. We recommend using a USB 2.0 hub which will allow the Balance Plate to stream at full sample rate.\nThere are no known issues as far as using the AMD 300 series chipsets with USB 3.0 devices.\nLast updated: 2025-11-13 | View on official support site",
